title: The Wiosna Project
subtitle: Standing work of a party that Wiosna now owns: the bridge to the liberal centre, the two bills, and the flank.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 140
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_wiosna_project_timer <= 0 and spring_path_stage >= 2
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_wiosna_project_timer = 4
card-image: img/poland/cards/programme-convention.webp

= The Wiosna Project

[? if spring_path_route = "social_liberal": The party is an equality-first
social-liberal Left and has stopped apologising for the second half of that
description. Its problem is that owning the argument is not the same as owning
a majority for it.?]
[? if spring_path_route = "market_liberal": **Ruch Postępu** is fiscally
conservative and socially liberal, and every week has to prove that this is a
project rather than a mood that worked once in 2011. Its problem is that both
halves of the sentence have a constituency that hates the other half.?]
[? if spring_path_route = "none": The doctrine convention has not reported.
Wiosna owns the leadership and the party still has two economic programmes and
one press office.?]

Bridge to the liberal centre: **[+ spring_liberal_bridge +]/100**. Economic
line: **[+ left_economic_position +]/100**. [? if razem_active = 1 and
razem_in_left = 1: Razem dissent: **[+ razem_dissent +]/100**.?][? if
razem_party_formed = 1: Razem is outside and on the ballot.?]

- @project_bridge
- @project_bills
- @project_business
- @project_floor
- @project_konf

@project_bridge
title: Work the liberal centre's social wing
subtitle: Private counting with KO and Poland 2050 deputies who already agree and never have to prove it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.spring_liberal_bridge += 8;
Q.ko_relation += 3;
Q.p2050_relation += 2;
Q.ko_accept_rights += 3;
Q.metropolitan_liberals_left_affinity += 1;
Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 1;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 3;
Q.razem_dissent += 2;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.news_headline = "The Left builds a standing channel to the liberal centre's social wing";
!}

The meetings are held in ones and twos and never announced. What comes out of
them is not an alliance but a list: the deputies who will vote for the bills
whatever their own leadership decides, and the ones who need to be able to say
they were persuaded late.

- #poland_card_finish

@project_bills
title: Push the two bills up the parliamentary timetable
subtitle: Committee work, drafting and public pressure on the people holding the calendar.
on-arrival: {!
Q.marriage_reform_progress += 4;
Q.abortion_reform_progress += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_salience += 4;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_salience += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_left_ownership += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_abortion_rights_left_ownership += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_lgbt_equality_backlash += 2;
Q.feminist_trust += 3;
Q.progressive_credibility += 2;
Q.psl_relation -= 2;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Proposal";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Parliamentary committee work";
Q.last_policy_implementation = 0;
Q.news_headline = "The rights bills move up the parliamentary timetable";
!}

Śmiszek's people spend the month on the unglamorous part: committee dates,
amendments drafted so the conservative objections have somewhere to go, and a
weekly count published to everybody who claims to support the bills and hopes
nobody is counting.

- #poland_card_finish

@project_business
title: Court the professionals and the self-employed
subtitle: Moves the economic line right. The professional vote arrives; the labour flank keeps its receipts.
choose-if: spring_path_route != "social_liberal"
unavailable-subtitle: The convention adopted an equality-first programme that does not open the economic line.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_economic_position += 3;
Q.left_right_score += 2;
Q.market_liberal_support += 6;
Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity += 3;
Q.metropolitan_liberals_left_affinity += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 6;
Q.razem_cooperation -= 4;
Q.labor_dissent += 5;
Q.labor_credibility -= 2;
Q.konf_poll_momentum -= 0.10;
Q.resources += 1;
Q.news_headline = "The Left spends the month with people who file their own invoices";
!}

Four regional business breakfasts, a donation list that no Left treasurer has
seen the like of since the 1990s, and a room full of people who want the two
bills passed and their contributions capped, in that order or the other one.

- #poland_card_finish

@project_floor
title: Reassure the labour flank
subtitle: Moves the economic line back left. Buys the flank at the price of the pitch.
on-arrival: {!
Q.left_economic_position -= 3;
Q.left_right_score -= 2;
Q.market_liberal_support -= 4;
Q.labor_dissent -= 7;
Q.labor_credibility += 4;
Q.workers_support += 2;
Q.public_sector_support += 2;
Q.razem_dissent -= 5;
Q.razem_cooperation += 4;
Q.liberal_professionals_left_affinity -= 1;
Q.spring_dissent += 2;
Q.news_headline = "The leadership spends a month reassuring the labour flank";
!}

Wage floors, inspection funding and a public appearance beside people in
uniforms that are not suits. Nothing in the doctrine is repudiated and every
sentence is chosen so the unions can quote it back later.

- #poland_card_finish

@project_konf
title: Take the freedom argument off Konfederacja
subtitle: Contest the young anti-system vote directly. Loud, effective and resented internally.
on-arrival: {!
Q.konf_poll_momentum -= 0.25;
Q.anti_establishment_youth_left_affinity += 3;
Q.young_support += 3;
Q.public_mood_pending_secular_state_left_ownership += 3;
Q.media_capacity += 2;
Q.konf_relation -= 5;
Q.razem_dissent += 3;
Q.labor_dissent += 2;
Q.news_headline = "The Left contests Konfederacja's young voters on their own ground";
!}

Streamed debates, a month of formats nobody in the leadership enjoys, and one
question asked repeatedly: a state small enough to leave you alone should be
small enough to leave everybody alone. It lands with exactly the audience it
was aimed at.

- #poland_card_finish
